    "reason": "Parent static review of the BASE protocol: SEPARABILITY_NOTE is informational, not an error. Add only bounded instrument guards against empty/duplicate/empty-expectation greens, preserve interrupted/unstarted cases, and authenticate real BASE/tool source pins. All 18 semantic inputs and v2 expectations are unchanged; no execution informed this revision."
  },
  "semantic_inputs_sha256": "f8ab48b76e6786fbba250ccc622a018b635c7bce146c5f373c19dd1b7f3e8a49",
  "semantic_output_contract": "Grade exit plus stable finding/error classification, owner edge, canonical target and citing location, or an explicit numeric zero-findings declaration. Human explanations, whitespace and summary wording are not expected values. SEPARABILITY_NOTE is known non-error information; retain it raw without grading its wording. Unknown, contradictory or unparseable output makes the ruler unevaluable (exit2), never green. Empty case sets, duplicate identities and empty/underspecified expectations are input errors. On Timeout/OSError preserve completed cases, the unsettled current case and remaining notObserved cases, emit exit2 and never retry. Ambiguity fail-closed is a specification requirement; these 18 inputs do not independently exercise every possible ambiguity.",
  "measurement_preconditions": "Resolve the oracle BASE as an actual commit through --lane's read-only Git object store before creating cases. Keep the resolved BASE distinct from the Parent-selected checker revision, expected SHA-256 and actual selected bytes; verify selected checker bytes against both the Parent digest and its landed Git blob. Plain-file WORKTREE inputs do not replace the real BASE store.",
  "prior_path_control": "The unchanged base-existing case names corpus/lessons/round-50.md, which exists in the real BASE Git tree. Its expected0 genuinely exercises the prior-path naming exemption even though the plain WORKTREE input changes that file's contents. It does not certify semantic independence of newly changed contents in a prior file."
